---
Title: The (…) argument slot
---

# The argument slot

A handler that declares `arg: true` takes a leading parenthesis:
@image(figs/a.png)[with an argument]{width=0.2} — and the block form puts the
`+` on the name, before the argument.

@image+(figs/b.png)[block form]{width=0.3}

Every other name leaves parentheses to prose. A registered name that did not ask
for an argument keeps its parenthetical — @span[styled]{.k}(like this one) — and
an unregistered @note(aside) is not a directive at all. An address such as
me@example.com is untouched, as is a bare @image with no argument of any kind.

A block form buried mid-sentence — @image+(figs/c.png)[oops] — is misplaced, and
says so.
